  "packageHash": "egPcmbYJOEH3o2QfmV1i2NyPddFlRnLTkGyt778sULvd4BCizziK/R6VKfoED/byG51xCAxQZK1TluaIkxbquw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 89677,
  "published": "2026-06-18T14:20:20.23Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0 preview: the node's static Create(RuntimeNodeFactoryContext …) factory moves into a dedicated internal *NodeFactory class, removing the public static Create from the node type (breaking). Node registration, options, ports, JSON shape, and runtime behavior are unchanged. Replaces the bespoke IMqttClock abstraction with System.TimeProvider (UseClock now takes a TimeProvider; the old clock interface/implementation are removed). Introduces a separate mqtt.connection resource component that owns the connection profile and reconnect policy; mqtt.publish/mqtt.subscribe now reference it by required connectionName and no longer carry connection/reconnect config. For now the connection holds configuration only — no client is established, so publish/subscribe report a not-connected result until a later connect step. Adds an explicit, host-driven connect lifecycle: mqtt.connection now exposes ConnectAsync/DisconnectAsync (plus a connection State and a lock-free TryGetAdapter), owning the single client lease and health monitor; mqtt.publish/mqtt.subscribe borrow the established adapter when connected (subscribe (re)subscribes on connect, deduped per connection epoch) and report not-connected otherwise, never connecting or disposing. No auto-connect.",
